+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static homepage with responsive layouts and browser-only signing for coffee receipts and gift vouchers. No build step or external JavaScript dependencies are required. Serve the files over HTTPS (or localhost) for Web Crypto access.
+
+## Signing and trust
+
+- Uses Web Crypto ECDSA P-256 with SHA-256. This is a classical asymmetric signature.
+- Generates a non-exportable private key and saves the CryptoKey pair in IndexedDB. Key creation is serialized across tabs.
+- Signs canonical JSON containing all document details, issuer metadata, timestamp, random document ID and public-key fingerprint.
+- Verification checks signatures against the public key already saved in this browser. Keys embedded in uploaded documents are never trusted.
+- Supports JSON downloads, file uploads, pasted JSON, recent document history, and public verification-key export. Documents stay local.
+
+This static site establishes a **local browser issuer**, not a certified Daily Grind merchant identity. Production merchant authenticity needs an independently provisioned issuer and a trusted public-key distribution mechanism. Exported public keys must be authenticated separately before another verifier trusts them. There is no payment processing or voucher redemption ledger: signing does not confirm payment, prevent repeated redemption, or establish a voucher balance. Clearing browser storage removes the signing key and history; download documents and export the public key before clearing it. The private key cannot be exported or backed up by this app.
+
+## Checks
+
+Run `npm test` for Web Crypto tests covering receipt/voucher signing, JSON round trips, changes to signed fields, unknown issuers, forged signatures and malformed documents. No server or browser is required for these tests.
